&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; BELLE MOREAU is suffocating under her overbearing fiance’s pressure to have a baby. To escape the next IVF appointment, she books a beach house on a remote barrier island, COROLLA, NC. On her way to Corolla, Belle stops by her controlling, abusive father’s assisted living home where he begs her to put him out of his misery and kill him. Conflicted by his pleas, she ignores her father’s request and goes to the house in Corolla. There she meets CHIP, the house’s human-run concierge who promises to remotely tend to her every need.


&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; After mercy killing her father, Belle relishes her newfound freedom, her new love, and her new thirst for murder.
